// mission's 14 languages, in the order of portal/i18n/catalogs.json: en de es fr pt uk ru it tr fa ro sv da ar.
//
// What it is: a template's slides are written for ONE language when the deck is made (the person picks it in the new
// presentation dialog; the portal's own language is the default), and every word on them comes from this table.
// Deck content is never translated afterwards, like the rest of Presentations (slidev/README.md). The names of
// numbers that a live chart draws itself come from portal-api in English; the templates draw their own legends and
// labels, so the slides are in one language from top to bottom.
// Who uses it: templates/index.mjs. slidev/tests/mmm-templates.test.mjs checks that every key has all 14 languages.
// Every language except English needs review by a native speaker, like the portal's own catalogs.

